 "notes": "Shelf \"Jeans\" rebuilt as one kind with 22 archetypes (125 versions) plus 20 leftover models in m (one representative per remaining notable brand). Old kind had 246 flat models. Changes: Levi's cut from 45 SKUs to five archetype families (501 with LVC era versions; 505/502; 517/527 bootcut; 511/510/512/513 slim; 550/559/555/568/541 relaxed) — other Levi's numbers (405, 412, 445, 454, 468, 469, 478, 506, 507, 514, 531, 537, 557, 565, 567, 569, 578, Extra Baggy) dropped as SKU noise. Lee 101Z Riders, Wrangler 13MWZ, A.P.C., Evisu Lot 2000, Nudie named fits and JNCO wide-leg (all old JNCO models kept as versions) made archetypes. Japanese houses organised as own house-cut archetypes (Warehouse, Sugar Cane, Full Count, TCB, Studio D'Artisan, Iron Heart, Samurai, Flat Head, Pure Blue Japan, Momotaro, Japan Blue) with their old models as versions, per Heddels guide. In m, each remaining brand reduced to one flagship model: Real McCoy's, Mister Freedom, ONI, Burgus Plus, Edwin 503, Big John, orSlow, Naked & Famous, 3sixteen, Tellason, Benzak, Indigofera, Diesel, True Religion, Fashion Box (Replay), AMIRI, Carhartt, Dickies, R.M. Williams, Ksenia Schnaider; second/third models of those brands (e.g. ONI 200/222/266/622, Naked & Famous Super/Easy/Strong/True/Groovy Guy, Diesel Sleenker/D-Vyl/Zatiny/D-Strukt, Pherrow's, Billy Reid, Mustang, Meltin' Pot, Liu Jo, Gardeur, Noko) dropped as SKU depth. \"Big E\" 501 and Flat Head 3005 omitted — not confirmed in any retrieved page. Dropped per brief: Carrera, Gas, Cecil, Mavi, Castro. Dropped as out of scope: motorcycle riding jeans (Bull-it, Pando Moto, Street & Steel — protective gear) and Vulpine cycling jeans (sport-specific apparel stays with its sport). Unconfirmed years left blank in versions. Sources: Wikipedia (Levi Strauss & Co., Lee, Wrangler, JNCO, Jeans, Japanese denim, Momotaro, Nudie, Evisu, A.P.C., Edwin, Big John, Diesel, True Religion), Gear Patrol Levi's fit guide, Levi Strauss 1967 archive post, Hypebeast 517 relaunch, Heddels (Lee history, Japanese denim guide, A.P.C. and Evisu posts), jnco.com product page. One tradition entry (Japanese selvedge denim) added.",
